    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 2,
    "bbox": [
      185.85,
      230.69,
      377.85,
      255.47
    ],
    "text": "AN ACT TO AMEND THE CODE OF CRIMINAL PROCEDURE(SPECIAL PROVISIONS) ACT, NO. 2 OF 2013",
    "fonts": [
      "Times"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      7.0,
      10.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 2,
    "bbox": [
      161.85,
      270.89,
      401.9,
      295.67
    ],
    "text": "BE it enacted by the Parliament of the Democratic SocialistRepublic of Sri Lanka as follows:\u2013",
    "fonts": [
      "Times"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      10.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 2,
    "bbox": [
      161.85,
      311.09,
      401.88,
      349.19
    ],
    "text": "1.This Act may be cited as the Code of CriminalProcedure (Special Provisions) (Amendment) Act,No. of 2017.",
    "fonts": [
      "Times",
      "TimesNewRoman,Bold"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      10.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 2,
    "bbox": [
      161.85,
      364.73,
      401.9,
      416.27
    ],
    "text": "2.The following new section is hereby insertedimmediately after section 6 of the Code of CriminalProcedure (Special Provisions) Act, No. 2 of 2013 and shallhave effect as section 6A of that Act:\u2013",
    "fonts": [
      "Times",
      "TimesNewRoman,Bold"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      7.0,
      10.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 2,
    "bbox": [
      215.85,
      431.69,
      401.89,
      550.19
    ],
    "text": "6A. (1) Notwithstanding anything to thecontrary in this Act, an Attorney-at-Lawrepresenting a person in police custody shall,from the time such person is taken into custody,be entitled to have access to the police stationin which such person is being held in custody,for the purpose of meeting the officer incharge of the police station and makingrepresentations to such officer.",
    "fonts": [
      "Times"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      7.0,
      10.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 2,
    "bbox": [
      215.85,
      565.73,
      401.89,
      630.59
    ],
    "text": "(2) The right of an Attorney-at-Law, to haveaccess to the police station, and to makerepresentations, shall not affect theinvestigations that may be conducted inrespect of the person being represented.",
    "fonts": [
      "Times"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      10.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 2,
    "bbox": [
      215.85,
      646.13,
      401.87,
      670.79
    ],
    "text": "(3) Any such Attorney-at-Law shall bepermitted entry into such police station and",
    "fonts": [
      "Times"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      10.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 2,
    "bbox": [
      407.85,
      365.71,
      449.13,
      413.18
    ],
    "text": "Insertion ofnew section6A in Act,No. 2 of2013.",
    "fonts": [
      "Times"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      5.599999904632568,
      8.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 2,
    "bbox": [
      144.57,
      577.97,
      155.01,
      589.31
    ],
    "text": "20",
    "fonts": [
      "Times"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      10.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 2,
    "bbox": [
      161.85,
      432.19,
      209.85,
      489.26
    ],
    "text": "\u201cRight of anAttorney-at-Law to accessa person inthe policecustody.",
    "fonts": [
      "Times"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      8.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 2,
    "bbox": [
      144.57,
      657.89,
      155.01,
      669.23
    ],
    "text": "25",
    "fonts": [
      "Times"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      10.0
    ]
  },
  {
